			<div class="content" id="post-content-4827150">
									

<p>Goo Goo Gaa Gaa, Baby Crit Ahead</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[Incomprehensible]</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Translation&nbsp;Complete</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>From the start, I say collapse the Central Narrative, that is way too long and just draws my eyes away from the rest. There is no button for it unfortunately, so just copy pasta it from the internet.</p>
<p>Your use of the word &quot;veil&quot; for 1, just confuses me. You may be using it in the right way, but I just find it confusing to read. Maybe consider changing it to guise, show, et cetera.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>leaving behind multiple anomalous object that point to the existance of a society of renaissance cognitohazard wizards.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>How do they point to wizards? a book with &quot;spells&quot; doesn't instantly point to wizards, you would need something more obvious. and why specifically renaissance? Unless you mean it by the resurgence of cognitohazard wizards, how would you get that information?</p>
<p>About the library, if it isn't anomalous, why doesn't the foundation just take the books and put them into a high value storage vault? If it is anomalous, whats stopping them from just bringing the library to a site and monitoring it?</p>
<p>This is an interesting concept, but I think it needs to flesh itself out a big more.</p>
<p>P.S. I don't do recrits so don't PM me please, thanks.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Angryman, awaaay</p>

